{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:13.20.700","page_type":"section"},"citation":"13.20.700","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.700","content_hash":"14f6d6c3573326d620775bbe63d54e5b5121b654b8fbcc2913a1102f6da5ec67","heading":"Standard classification charges.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.20.700:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.700","text":"(a) For the purpose of calculating wastewater service charges, the minimum standard classification charge shall be based upon the average strength of domestic wastewater, and for this purpose the average strength of domestic wastewater is hereby defined as containing not more than the following:\nThree hundred mg/l suspended solids (SS);\nFour hundred mg/l chemical oxygen demand (COD);\nThree hundred mg/l biochemical oxygen demand (BOD);\nFifty mg/l oil and grease (O&G) (animal or vegetable origin);\nTen mg/l phosphorus (P);\nThirty mg/l Kjeldahl nitrogen;\nSeven hundred mg/l total solids (TS);\nAdditional elements of wastewater strength as may be deemed necessary by the Director.\n(b) Any person desiring to discharge wastewater to the City sewage collection system having a concentration greater than 300 mg/l suspended solids or 300 mg/l biochemical oxygen demand shall receive written permission from the Director before allowing such discharge. (Ord. 19496 § 91, 12-21-10; Ord. 18272 § 9, 6-22-04. Code 1995 § 146-343. Formerly 14.80.790.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"12032ae7-7292-5b58-8c8c-63122d42cb59"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.20.700","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.20.700","content_hash":"e11a60b26ea04b333b8d746068c1b28e1b6256d47e4f68affbfaf0